commit d4ba9808b9fb4dab4cb5c420fe0d88d76661568e

C03: a prohibition acknowledgement may name the PC and conjugate the prohibited verb (NEGATIVE1431)

NEGATIVE1429 measured «jamás apagues la pc» and «No apagues la PC.»: the model answered «Entendido, nunca apagaré la PC.» and the shaped-presentation contract rejected it twice, so the turn fell back to a semantic clarification. _unsupported_answer_mentions_request keeps only request tokens of three letters or more (the acronym «pc» vanished) and compares exact tokens («apagues» ≠ «apagaré»).

llm._unsupported_answer_mentions_request: the two-letter device tokens «pc», «tv» and «ip» count as request concepts, and a five-letter stem shared by a request token and an answer token counts as a mention. Offline probe: the two rejected acknowledgements pass; an unrelated answer and a bare «Entendido.» are still rejected. Mind only. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


